<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8cefea24d474> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 day after Weintraub shared the video, Cruise commented on the clip, stating its vehicle yielded to police and moved to the nearest safe location for that traffic stop." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1419" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aac5b2393213> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "GM’s Cruise vehicles have been operating autonomously in San Francisco at night, giving rides to employees around the city." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1364" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0bd1b3b7bacc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Since February, GM’s Cruise self-driving unit has offered public taxi rides in San Francisco." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1419" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9233cffde6c8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "B.rad916 posted a clip on Instagram of a self-driving car belonging to General Motors' Cruise line interacting with San Francisco Police Department officers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1418" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f78c1c65a215> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The car, owned and operated by a company called Cruise in San Francisco, is based on a Chevy Bolt chassis - although the company plans to launch a completely original vehicle soon." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1417" .

